From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: release the MI2S clock across system
 sleep

The MI2S bit clock is taken when a back end starts up and given back when
it shuts down, so a stream left open when the system sleeps keeps it
enabled. The clock is a DSP (q6prm) clock, and the DSP keeps the SoC's
XO running for it. The card had no PM ops either, so ASoC never suspended
its PCMs or DAPM.

On the AYANEO Pocket VERT, PipeWire still had the speaker open from
Steam's UI sound when the power button suspended the device, and the SoC
never reached AOSS sleep, CX collapse or DDR low power in s2idle.
Suspended from a shell with the speaker closed, it spent 78.7 of 80
seconds in all three.

Use the ASoC PM ops, give the clock back once the card is suspended and
take it again before the card resumes. DAPM powers the amps back up after
that, with the bit clock running, and PCM operations wait for the card to
be back at D0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -275,6 +275,35 @@
 	qcom_snd_sdw_shutdown(substream);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A stream open across system sleep keeps the MI2S clock enabled, and with it
+ * the SoC's XO. The PCMs and DAPM (the amps) are suspended by now, and
+ * resume_pre runs before DAPM powers the amps back up.
+ */
+static int sc8280xp_snd_suspend_post(struct snd_soc_card *card)
+{
+	struct sc8280xp_snd_data *pdata = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(card);
+
+	if (pdata->mi2s_clk_count)
+		clk_disable_unprepare(pdata->i2s_clk);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int sc8280xp_snd_resume_pre(struct snd_soc_card *card)
+{
+	struct sc8280xp_snd_data *pdata = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(card);
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	if (pdata->mi2s_clk_count) {
+		ret = clk_prepare_enable(pdata->i2s_clk);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_err(card->dev, "failed to restart the MI2S clock: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 				     struct snd_pcm_hw_params *params)
 {
@@ -490,6 +519,8 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(data->i2s_clk), "unable to get i2s clock\n");
 
 	card->driver_name = data->priv->driver_name;
+	card->suspend_post = sc8280xp_snd_suspend_post;
+	card->resume_pre = sc8280xp_snd_resume_pre;
 	sc8280xp_add_be_ops(card);
 	return devm_snd_soc_register_card(dev, card);
 }
@@ -666,6 +697,7 @@
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "snd-sc8280xp",
 		.of_match_table = snd_sc8280xp_dt_match,
+		.pm = &snd_soc_pm_ops,
 	},
 };
 module_platform_driver(snd_sc8280xp_driver);
